The file voc.txt was produced from a dump of the Croatian Wikipedia
(hrwiki-latest-pages-articles.xml.bz2, downloaded on 2026-10-07): 60000 articles drawn at random (seed 1) from the dump,
with wiki markup removed.

29974 words were selected, consisting only of the letters a-z, c-caron,
c-acute, d-stroke, s-caron and z-caron (at least two letters), lower-cased and
sorted. About 90% are the most frequent words of the sample that are known to
the hunspell hr_HR dictionary (LibreOffice dictionaries, used only as a
filter; no word list was copied from it; at least 23 occurrences), and the
rest are the most frequent other words (names, foreign words, new words; at
least 20 occurrences). Markup leftovers such as colour codes were removed.
Proper nouns, words from other languages and typos are included on purpose.

output.txt was generated from voc.txt by running it through the stemmer using the command:

stemwords -l croatian -c UTF_8 -i croatian/voc.txt -o croatian/output.txt

